    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate prioritizing top-of-order run creators and speed-demon opportunists. **James Wood** (70.96) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (70.58) lead the charge as our strongest plays, with **Wood** leveraging a lead-off spot against a middling Bradley to maximize his elite xwOBA potential. **Corbin Carroll** (70.10) remains a must-start, as his ability to disrupt on the basepaths is essential for our SB-weighted strategy, even against a decent arm like Chandler. Meanwhile, **Seiya Suzuki** (68.46) benefits from a favorable matchup against Abbott; the combination of a positive park factor and a slow pitcher delivery makes him a high-efficiency engine for today\u2019s production.\n\nWe are keeping a close watch on **Trevor Story** (62.04) and **Zach McKinstry** (59.51), both of whom are buoyed by wind-out conditions and favorable matchups that elevate their upside beyond standard projections. **Story** is particularly enticing due to the high likelihood of stolen base opportunities against a left-hander with a slower delivery. On the bench, **Alex Freeland** (40.41) was the final cut, narrowly missing the starting cutline. While **Freeland** offers switch-hitting versatility, the optimizer favored the higher ceiling of our starters against more vulnerable pitchers. We are also monitoring the total washout of **Mickey Moniak**, which forced us to shuffle our OF depth, and exercising caution with **Jose Caballero** (39.32), who was benched primarily due to a brutal matchup against deGrom that cratered his efficiency score well below our 40-point floor. \n\nThe primary risk remains the volatility of our lower-scored starters, specifically **Austin Riley** (47.22) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (46.35), both of whom face elite-tier arms in Kirby and S\u00e1nchez. **Soderstrom** in particular is flirting with our bench threshold; if his game-day environment worsens, he remains the most vulnerable piece of the current rotation. With **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Brice Turang**, **Max Muncy**, **Kyle Karros**, and **Carson Williams** all waiting in the wings or currently providing depth, we have the flexibility to pivot if any of our active starters see their lineup status or weather outlook shift before first pitch.",
